# Rebuild missing FX_Receptii_H / FX_Receptii rows from FX_Istoric (slice 0062).
#
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), open this file and
# click "Send Request" above each block, IN ORDER. The password is asked in a prompt and
# never written here. The token from step 2 is captured automatically into {{login.response.body.Token}}.
#
# Local server instead of production: change @host (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:5000).

@host = https://kbot.avatarsoft.ro
@username = scavatarsoft@gmail.com
@cod = AAB37CNBK95
# ADMIN blocks only (bottom of the file): the database name and the server key. Do NOT
# commit a real key here -- put it in a REST Client environment ($shared / settings) instead.
@dbname = 000_DEMO
@apikey = <API_KEY din config.py>

### 1. Which units (DC) can this user open?  -> pick the DC you want in step 2
# @prompt password Parola
# @name units
POST {{host}}/api/auth/units
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Login on ONE unit (db_name = the DC from step 1) -> bearer token
# @prompt password Parola
# @prompt dc DC-ul unitatii (din pasul 1)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}", "db_name": "{{dc}}", "machine": "VSCODE" }

### 3. DRY RUN - counts only, writes nothing (aplica = false)
POST {{host}}/api/forexe/receptii/refacere
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cod": "{{cod}}", "aplica": false }

### 4. APPLY - writes, in one transaction (aplica = true). Run 3 first and read the numbers.
POST {{host}}/api/forexe/receptii/refacere
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cod": "{{cod}}", "aplica": true }

### 3b. WHOLE DATABASE, dry run: every angajament with receptie history, counts only.
# `detalii` lists only the angajamente where something is missing or worth a warning;
# `erori` lists the ones that failed (each angajament is its own transaction).
POST {{host}}/api/forexe/receptii/refacere
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toate": true, "aplica": false }

### 4b. WHOLE DATABASE, apply. One commit per angajament; a failing one is rolled back
# alone and reported in `erori`, the rest still get written. Run 3b first.
POST {{host}}/api/forexe/receptii/refacere
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "toate": true, "aplica": true }

### 5. Check: the receptii list now includes the rebuilt snapshots (idrr = null while unplaced)
GET {{host}}/api/forexe/receptii?cod={{cod}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.Token}}

### ADMIN, no login: the server-wide key (config.py API_KEY) + the database name in the body.
# Same body and same answer as above, plus "db_name" echoed back. Dry run:
POST {{host}}/api/admin/receptii/refacere
X-Api-Key: {{apikey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "db_name": "{{dbname}}", "toate": true, "aplica": false }

### ADMIN, whole database, APPLY
POST {{host}}/api/admin/receptii/refacere
X-Api-Key: {{apikey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "db_name": "{{dbname}}", "toate": true, "aplica": true }

### ADMIN, one angajament, dry run
POST {{host}}/api/admin/receptii/refacere
X-Api-Key: {{apikey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "db_name": "{{dbname}}", "cod": "{{cod}}", "aplica": false }

### 6. Logout (optional)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.Token}}
